# Production build values.
#
# This fork has no cloud backend: every model call goes straight from Zotero to
# a provider with your own key, and nothing authenticates against Supabase. But
# the inherited auth component still constructs a Supabase client on mount, and
# getSupabaseConfig() throws on an empty URL — so a bundle built without these
# dies on load, taking the whole React tree with it. That is exactly what
# shipping 0.1.19 did: `npm run build` looks for `.env.production`, did not find
# one, compiled empty strings, and the plugin would not start.
#
# These are the same inert placeholders `.env.development` uses. Nothing
# connects to them; they exist so the client can be constructed and ignored.
# Keep this file in step with `.env.development` — both are gitignored, so a
# fresh clone gets them from `.env.production.example` instead.

SUPABASE_URL=http://localhost:54321
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<same placeholder as .env.development>
API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
WEBAPP_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000